  "claims": [
    "one composable treeReadWindow function consumes an explicit transaction and catalog without writer or format changes",
    "absolute half-open occurrence ranks intersect typed scalar or complete key cuts with stable source/slot ties",
    "count-pruned BFS batches independent frontier child probes, caches each fetched node once and scatters outputs by rank without sorting",
    "O(log(n+1)+k) valid-tree node work and O(k) output assembly with bounded comparison/encoding assumptions",
    "explicit finite configurable node, batch, logical encoded-byte and output budgets; whole-call rejection, no partial successful frontier",
    "loaded identity, local link and expanded count/height/balance/ancestor-order checks; no writes or namespace scans",
    "adjacent rank windows and exclusive complete cuts compose under one adapter snapshot",
    "queued writer cannot mix versions into an in-flight memory-adapter reader"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "raw counts and member identities are privileged; no source hydration, authentication, authorization or visible rank acceptance",
    "JS-P4b owner-stream composition and JS-P4c serialized cursor fencing remain unaccepted",
    "continuation composes only within a single snapshot; separate read callbacks may observe changed state",
    "logical encoded-byte accounting happens after eager getMany cloning, not a hard heap, network-transfer or prefetch byte bound",
    "finite batch capacity adds storage calls; processing waves exclude header/head setup and do not measure network RTT or wall time",
    "pruned subtree metadata is trusted; independent checkStore remains required for full structural and inventory verification",
    "memory adapter is local serialized and volatile; no durable, distributed, production or native-suite acceptance implied"
  ],
